  <LanguagePacks><LanguagePack ID="ENU" IsDefault="true"><DisplayStrings><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.FileServices.HostParticipation"><Name>Hyper-V Host SMB Storage Participation</Name><Description>Present only on Hyper-V hosts that actually store virtual hard disks on an SMB/UNC path. File Services monitoring targets this object, so hosts with no UNC-backed storage are never evaluated.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.FileServices.SmbReport.Task"><Name>Show SMB client and share report</Name><Description>SMB services, client connections with dialect and CA state, multichannel paths and RDMA capability, witness registrations, signing/encryption posture, local shares and VHDX files on UNC paths.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.FileServices.SmbLatency.Task"><Name>Show SMB client latency and connectivity events</Name><Description>SMB Client Shares latency, queue and credit-stall counters plus the latest SMB client connectivity events.</Description></DisplayString><DisplayString ElementID="HyperVPrivateCloud.Capability.FileServices.Task.WriteAction"><Name>FileServices task runner</Name><Description>Runs the operator task script for this capability through PowerShell 7 on the agent and returns its text output.</Description></DisplayString>{{ELEMENT_DISPLAY_STRINGS}}{{FILE_SERVICES_DISPLAY_STRINGS}}
